WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.510
- [Instructor] What we're
going to do in this video

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:05.250
is to start thinking about
adding mixed numbers.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:07.640
Now just as a reminder of
what a mixed number is,

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:11.900
it'd be something like three and 2/8.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.640
It's called mixed because part of the way

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.650
we represent this number
is there's a whole number,

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:19.720
the three, and then part
is as a fraction, 2/8.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.510
But the numbers three and 2/8ths.

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:24.380
So let's think about how
we might be able to add

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:29.380
three and 2/8ths to five and 3/8ths.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.670
So pause this video and see
if you can have a go at this

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:39.050
before we work through this together.

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:40.750
All right, now let's work
through this together.

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.550
Now there's a couple of ways
that we could approach this.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:47.160
You might recognize that three
and 2/8ths is the same thing

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:52.160
as three plus 2/8ths, and five and 3/8ths

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:57.620
is the same thing as five plus 3/8ths.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:00:59.850
And so if we add these two things together

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:03.750
we're just adding really
these four things together

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:06.410
and the order in which
we add doesn't matter

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:11.050
so you could view this as three plus five

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:17.190
plus 2/8ths plus 2/8ths, plus 3/8ths,

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.300
notice it's just the same thing,

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.920
I'm just changing the order with which

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:26.330
we are adding, and now
what is three plus five?

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:28.200
Three wholes plus five wholes,

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.140
we'll that's just going to be eight.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:34.530
And then what is 2/8ths plus 3/8ths?

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:36.930
Well if I have two of
something, in this case eighths,

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:39.250
and I add three more of that something,

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:40.900
in this case eighths, I'm gonna have five

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.700
of that something, in this case 5/8ths.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:46.920
So this is going to be eight plus 5/8ths.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:49.320
Which we can express as a mixed number

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:54.320
as just being equal to eight and 5/8ths.

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:57.770
Now there's other ways that you might see

00:01:57.770 --> 00:01:59.690
folks approaching this.

00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:01.390
You might see something like this

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:06.340
where people will write three plus 2/8ths

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:08.400
and then they will write right below that

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.870
they'll write the five in the ones place,

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:12.770
or in the whole number and
there's only a ones place

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:14.803
in these whole numbers,
so you'd write the five

00:02:14.803 --> 00:02:17.870
right below the three and then plus

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:20.850
and then the fraction you'd
write right below the fraction.

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:21.723
3/8ths.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:26.720
And then we can add vertically like this

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:29.400
where first we can look
at the fractional part,

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:34.400
2/8ths plus 3/8ths is
going to be equal to 5/8ths

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:40.990
and then three plus five is
going to be equal to eight

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:42.620
and if you add these two together,

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:45.740
eight and 5/8ths, you get eight and 5/8s.

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:47.360
So different ways to approach it,

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:50.050
but that will hopefully
start to get you comfortable

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:52.153
with adding a mixed numbers.

